// The same source as `tsconfig.json`, minus the DOM. `tsconfig.json` has to keep
// `"DOM"` for `builtin-plugins/vanilla-support/**`, which is browser code, and a
// `lib` applies to a whole program — so with one program a browser global is
// legal everywhere, and `document` in `collect/` compiles and throws under Node.
//
// Two files are excluded because they genuinely own DOM globals: `dom/env.ts`
// builds the jsdom environment, and `collect/worker.ts` runs after
// `createDomEnv()` has populated `globalThis`, so `document` there is real. The
// boundary is that function's reach, not a directory.
//
// Excluding them only works because `collect/types.ts` exists. `exclude` does
// not outrank an import, and `collect/index.ts` and `collect/task.ts` used to
// take `Payload` and `ReturnData` from `worker.js` — which pulled `worker.ts`
// back in, and `dom/env.ts` and `@types/jsdom` with it. `@types/jsdom` opens
// with `/// <reference lib="dom" />`, and a `reference lib` loads that lib
// whatever `lib` says here, so one type-only import undid the whole file.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": [
      "ESNext"
    ]
  },
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "generated/**/*",
    "dist/**/*",
    "src/**/__tests__/**",
    "src/node/builtin-plugins/vanilla-support/**",
    "src/node/collect/worker.ts",
    "src/node/dom/env.ts"
  ]
}
